      "confidence": "★",
      "effect": "~1.00x from four independent loop-side closures: +20 loop instructions gave 0.00%, deleting 22.5% of loop VALU gave +0.05%, scheduler and pipeline-scheduler flips spanned -3.2% to +0.1%, and doubling the M tile regressed -4.44% (per-case -8.8% and -5.0% on the two large-concurrency shapes)",
      "verified_on": "2026-08-12",
      "attempts": 1,
      "confirms_cited": 0,
      "confirms_blind": 0,
      "losses": 0,
      "last_seen": "2026-08-12",
      "title": "Loop-side axes are one closed axis when the loop is latency-bound",
      "lever": "When the main loop is latency-limited on the ds_read/global-load to MFMA chain across its barriers, treat instruction count, scheduling, occupancy, LDS and tile shape as one axis and price the whole axis with a cheap bracket instead of spending a round on each.",
      "apply": "The bracket is two experiments: add instructions to the loop at zero resource cost, then delete a fifth of its VALU while holding LDS traffic identical. Two readings of ~1.00x close the axis and hand the budget to another region.",
      "verify": "Run both arms against the frozen baseline with interleaved controls and inspect whether the sign flips between A/B pairs; one direction alone reads like a small win.",
      "pitfall": "targeting one more wave per SIMD drove the allocator below the pure-data live-set size -> hundreds of spills and reloads and a large scratch growth -> compute the live set first; that step can then be closed arithmetically at zero GPU cost\n  - pitfall: the small-concurrency case was modelled as DRAM-streaming-bound for most of the run -> a hardware counter undercounted DRAM traffic ~1.7x -> it is cache-residency-bound: 1.67x more B-tile reads cost only +13.7% where streaming predicts +67%",
      "caution": "Also verify the scale-block constants before concluding the tile shape is free: when they equal the K and N tile sizes those dimensions are welded, so a sweep can only move M - and M was already at the minimum of a clean U here.",
      "source": "run moe_stage1-own16h, 2026-08-12 - 13-round campaign, director-validated"
    }
